{"propaByan samarTaByam": [{"id": "propAByAM samarTAByAm", "headword": "प्रोपाभ्यां समर्थाभ्याम्", "headword_slp1": "propAByAM samarTAByAm", "fold": "propaByan samarTaByam", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "After the verb क्रम् preceded by वि , the आत्मनेपद is used when it is preceded by प्र and उप , both conveying the same sense; viz. that of 'beginning an action'.\n\nTerms: आत्मनेपद", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["प्रोपाभ्यां समर्थाभ्याम् १.३.४२", "१.३.४२", "१.३.४२ प्रोपाभ्यां समर्थाभ्याम्"], "synonyms_slp1": ["propAByAM samarTAByAm १.३.४२", "१.३.४२", "१.३.४२ propAByAM samarTAByAm"]}], "propaByan yujerayajYapatresu": [{"id": "propAByAM yujerayajYapAtrezu", "headword": "प्रोपाभ्यां युजेरयज्ञपात्रेषु", "headword_slp1": "propAByAM yujerayajYapAtrezu", "fold": "propaByan yujerayajYapatresu", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "After the verb युज् 'to join', the आत्मनेपद is used, when it is preceded by प्र and उप except with reference to sacrificial vessels even when the fruit of the action does not accrue to the agent.\n\nTerms: आत्मनेपद", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["प्रोपाभ्यां युजेरयज्ञपात्रेषु १.३.६४", "१.३.६४", "१.३.६४ प्रोपाभ्यां युजेरयज्ञपात्रेषु"], "synonyms_slp1": ["propAByAM yujerayajYapAtrezu १.३.६४", "१.३.६४", "१.३.६४ propAByAM yujerayajYapAtrezu"]}], "proktaluk": [{"id": "proktAlluk", "headword": "प्रोक्ताल्लुक्", "headword_slp1": "proktAlluk", "fold": "proktaluk", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "After the title of a work which is named after the Announcer thereof the affixes denoting 'who studies or who knows that' are elided by लुक् ।\n\nTerms: लुक्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["प्रोक्ताल्लुक् ४.२.६४", "४.२.६४", "४.२.६४ प्रोक्ताल्लुक्"], "synonyms_slp1": ["proktAlluk ४.२.६४", "४.२.६४", "४.२.६४ proktAlluk"]}]}